summary:
  The capture's end sends the writer a kill it cannot answer.

history:
  ffmpeg answers an interrupt by closing the segment it is cutting and
  ending its own list; killed outright it leaves a segment half written, and
  its command reports a death where there was an orderly end.

target:
  package/contents/ui/SlideLogic.js

find:
  " && kill -INT \"$p\" 2>/dev/null; true # " + a.seq;

replace:
  " && kill -KILL \"$p\" 2>/dev/null; true # " + a.seq;

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_slidelogic.qml::test_the_end_of_a_capture_signals_the_writer_and_removes_nothing.
